{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1475352-scion-2e-on-roll20-vtt","id":1475352,"title":"Scion 2E on Roll20 VTT!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-23T13:39:27-08:00","id":1475352,"title":"Scion 2E on Roll20 VTT!","content":"Scion 2E FINALLY at Roll20 VTT platform! \u2764\ufe0f<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/now-available-polyphemus-plus-scion-on-roll20/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/now-available-polyphemus-plus-scion-on-roll20/\" target=\"_blank\"> Now Available: Polyphemus, plus Scion on roll20! &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/now-available-polyphemus-plus-scion-on-roll20/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/now-available-polyphemus-plus-scion-on-roll20/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T14:11:29-08:00","id":1475356,"title":"","content":"I maybe blind - but the official Roll20 sheet do not have support for Antagonists use different stats blocks - with Dicepools, Health, etc? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Prove me that I'm wrong...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-23T17:54:36-08:00","id":1475381,"title":"","content":"On the one hand, having an official sheet on Roll20 is a good thing, and I\u2019m glad they\u2019ve put the work in. My two main groups have both expressed some interest in Scion, and we mainly use Roll20. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, I see we\u2019re back to using the Storytelling terms for the approaches instead of the Storypath ones, effectively spreading the goof on the Scion: Origin sheet to all the Roll20 sheets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-24T08:16:59-08:00","id":1475407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1475352-scion-2e-on-roll20-vtt?p=1475356#post1475356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I maybe blind - but the official Roll20 sheet do not have support for Antagonists use different stats blocks - with Dicepools, Health, etc? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Prove me that I'm wrong...</div> </div> </div> </div>The one OP just released has an option for Antagonists, with everything you mentioned.<br /> <br /> My comments...<br /> <br /> <b>Momentum</b>: I really don't know why this is on the sheet since this is a shared resource for the whole Band. Unless it auto-updates across all sheets it doesn't make sense to track this individually except as an optional house rule.<br /> <br /> <b>Attributes</b>: As someone else pointed out, the approaches have the wrong names.<br /> <br /> <b>Rolls</b>: I like how the roll system works a lot, having enhancement and difficulty as part of the dialogue box is great! One thing missing is the ability to add extra dice. Momentum and Paths can both add dice to a pool.<br /> <br /> <b>Health</b>: There isn't an option for adding Hard Armor levels, just Bruised, Injured, and Maimed.<br /> <br /> <b>Defense Roll</b>: I can't seem to change the value for the Defense roll, not sure if this is meant to auto update based on the highest Resilience Attribute or what.<br /> <br /> <b>Deeds</b>: I really love how it keeps track of completed Deeds. I try to do this for my table as a sense of the growing legend of the Band but its so easy to forget. The interaction between Deeds and Completed Deeds is buggy as hell. When you complete one Deed it reoutinely moves two down into completed. If you create a new Long term deed it tends to clear the value of a previous long term deed. To be usable this needs some work.<br /> <br /> <b>Paths</b>: I really like how these are handled! I love how there is a spot for Obligation, and a handy way to track if the Path have been invoked, suspended, etc...<br /> <br /> <b>Purviews &amp; Boons</b>: It might be handy to have a spot for the Innate power under the description. The dice icon for Clash doesn't do anything and appears to be broken. Also I'm not sure what the vs is meant to handle. Seemingly it would create two dice pools from the character's own traits to roll against each other?<br /> <br /> <b>Callings &amp; Knacks</b>: The dice icon doesn't appear to do anything, and what I think it is trying to do doesn't make sense. If you hover over the icon it says it wants to roll the Calling rating, which you don't really do outside of Clash rolls, and then you roll the higher of your Legend or Calling + a Knack Skill (or Integrity). It also seems weird there isn't an option for just rolling a Knack Skill built into the Knack box since some have that as an activation roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Birthrights</b>: These are solid, my only note is it might be nice to have a Description for them so you can jot in some of the flavor, but not really a requirement since you can store stuff like that in handouts in roll20.<br /> <br /> <br /> I hope the bugs gets fixed soon, I'd love to use this for my game but it's not quite there yet as opposed to the other options.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-24T09:35:49-08:00","id":1475410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1475352-scion-2e-on-roll20-vtt?p=1475407#post1475407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The one OPP just released has an option for Antagonists, with everything you mentioned.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Thiago pointed to me on Facebook this - To get proper Scion 2E support in Roll20, and sections like Antagonists also - you need to choose <i>'Character Sheet Template: Storypath by Onyx Path'</i> on game creation - it's official sheet that works. ( Scion 2E listed there is old fan made. )<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/ZrqQyBV.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> And the sheet itself overlook... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: 