s it compare to the unofficial sheet already on there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-24T17:21:08-08:00","id":1475423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1475352-scion-2e-on-roll20-vtt?p=1475419#post1475419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does it compare to the unofficial sheet already on there?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We've been using the unofficial one for over a year for my game. The official one does some stuff better, I think Paths are much better, and I like that Birthrights have sections for type specific info. The rolling mechanic is better in that you can factor in the difficulty and enhancement, and it'll tell you how much is left over. It supports Antagonists at all, which is pretty great.<br /> <br /> The deeds section being buggy is a big issue in the current state, and kind of deal breaker for me since I've seen it delete the text of deeds. Like the unofficial one it has no way to factor in bonus dice from Momentum or Paths, so you're left trying to find a combo of skill and attribute with the right amount of dice or use the roll20 dice roller for the extra dice or those rolls. There are a few other bugs that are more annoying than deal breaking that I detailed above.<br /> <br /> Once the bugs are fixed I'll probably convert my game to using it. If they don't fix the bugs I don't think it will be worth it since it shows they're not going to have any ongoing support and the bugs are annoying enough I don't feel a need to work around them when there is an ok alternative.<br /> <br /> Truthfully I'm waiting for Role to add in support for Story- path, teller, telling type systems where you roll a combo of two stats for a dice pool to their template library then I'll probably move off of roll20. It's a good tool, but it feels like it was made by software devs for software devs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T08:39:22-07:00","id":1486771,"title":"","content":"I have a very large complaint over this Roll20 implication for Scion 2E - I cannot roll using Antagonists variants of sheet, with their <b>Primary</b>, <b>Secondary</b>, <b>Desperation Pool</b> - or even <b>Initiative</b> for them. All the time I need to write /roll xd10&gt;8! \ud83d\ude21","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}